WEBVTT

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.530
I can't believe we were turned away
at five different bed and breakfasts.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:40.200
Because we keep telling them our real ages.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:44.360
But at least we managed to get
to a clothing store before it closed.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:45.490
This jacket is so warm.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:51.860
I feel kind of bad.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.320
You shouldn't. They're our first matching outfits.

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:57.280
Yeah.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.280
So what do we do now?

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:24.200
Er, um, do you rent out rooms here?
Could we stay the night-

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.780
We're closed today.

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:29.490
I see. Sorry for bothering you.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.320
Hmm, I guess we were a little too spontaneous.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:40.280
And now we're not going to make the last train.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:41.360
I'm sorry!

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:44.070
Come on, Tsutsun, you've been apologizing all night.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:45.530
Don't worry.

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:48.320
Worse comes to worst, we'll just wait
at the station until morning.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:53.570
Hey, come on back here.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:56.530
If you just need a place to sleep, you can stay.

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:57.990
A-are you sure?

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:00.490
We're still minors, is that okay?

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:02.450
I don't need to know that!

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:03.780
Just get in here.

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:24.570
Crying in a place like this,

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:30.570
No one will notice me. I know that

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:34.280
As if nothing ever happened,

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:39.990
The world alone moves forward, erasing the past

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:44.820
Even though I decided to photograph you on that film

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:49.320
The bottomless sky keeps accumulating

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:51.360
We may forget, but it doesn't disappear

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:54.070
That pain, remember? What was it?

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:59.740
If we get lost in the changing scenery,

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:03.900
We could try remembering that song

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:09.450
Yes, if we're together, even the sad things

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:13.240
Should eventually become treasures

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:22.360
I want to show you that you blended into the background

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:27.740
But didn't fade away that day

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:41.820
Episode 22
Regarding My Thoughts
on the Sacred Mysteries of Life.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:44.900
It's so good!

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:47.820
We're closed, so that's all I have to offer.

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:52.400
This is "all"? But it's like a fancy luxury meal!

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:53.900
This rice is amazing!

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.780
You think so? Well, rice is something we got plenty of.

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:58.450
You want a drink?

00:03:58.450 --> 00:03:59.700
Uh, no, thanks.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:04.610
Wow, that's pretty responsible
for a punk kid wandering the streets at night.

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:06.700
You running away from home or something?

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:10.570
Uh... no, not running away. But thanks for your help.

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:13.240
Sorry to bother you on your day off.

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:15.820
It's fine, I was bored.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:23.200
The missus ran out on me not too long ago.
And I can't run an inn all by myself.

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:27.780
Uh, am I supposed to laugh, too?

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:31.030
B-but if she doesn't come back, isn't that bad?

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:34.030
Eh, everything will be fine! This happens all the time.

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:36.490
It happens... all the time?

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:38.570
So are you two a couple?

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:42.400
You're such a total babe,
why are you dating such a plain-looking loser?

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:46.360
Let me guess, she's your first love, isn't she?

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:48.240
What?! Uh, yes, sir.

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:50.860
Seriously, why are you dating this guy?

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:52.530
I can hear you, you know...

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:57.490
But man, young kids...

00:04:57.490 --> 00:05:03.360
My first love was ages ago. Seeing you experience it in
the present progressive tense, you're making me jealous.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:05.200
You better enjoy it!

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.280
Oh, you finished your bath first.

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:16.070
Yeah.

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:19.400
That old man just talked and talked until he passed out.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:23.200
He says some mean things, but he's a nice guy.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:25.400
He even got baths ready for us.

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:27.320
I really liked the open-air bath.

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:29.360
I stayed in until I was almost cooked.

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:32.360
Oh! I'll go buy us some drinks.

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:33.450
Okay.

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:50.780
I want to sleep with Tsutsun.

00:05:56.900 --> 00:05:59.860
Wow! There are so many stars!

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:00.900
Yeah.

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:03.570
Wh-what's wrong? Are you cold?

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:07.030
No, I think I'm hot and cold.

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:09.320
Wait a minute! It sounds like
you're coming down with something!

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:11.450
Hold on, I'll get out the futons!

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:14.740
Hurry, get in!

00:06:15.110 --> 00:06:16.110
Okay...

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:22.360
Thank you, Tsutsun.

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:26.820
Tsutsun?

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:30.900
You wrote that you wanted to sleep with me.

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:32.820
Oh, you found that?

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:33.820
Yeah.

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:37.320
If you have a cold, this time, I'll take it from you.

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:40.610
Just like when we first met.

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:43.450
That takes me back.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:47.900
At first, before I got to know you, I thought...

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:49.610
you were terrible.

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:51.900
That's awful.

00:06:57.650 --> 00:07:00.700
Oh, I was just noticing how beautiful you are.

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:08.200
The truth is...

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:10.780
somewhere in my heart, I knew.

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:14.030
This girl doesn't have asthma.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:16.780
But I was scared.

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:19.610
I was afraid to look at the facts.

00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:24.070
I just couldn't bring myself to face that pain.

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:31.490
Can I memorize...

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:34.360
the shape of her features?

00:07:39.530 --> 00:07:40.740
I love you.

00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:44.740
I love you hundreds of times
more than when I first met you.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:49.150
Tsutsun?

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:50.740
Me, too.

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:23.700
Oh man...

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:25.650
This is insane...!

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:28.990
It's like every cell in my body has been reborn!

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:39.990
Look, I said I was sorry!

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:42.610
Please come home.

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:43.990
What?

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:46.570
I... I do love you!

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:49.780
Hey! What makes you think you can listen in?!

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:55.110
I-I hope your wife comes back, sir.

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:57.070
Just shut up and eat!

00:08:57.650 --> 00:09:00.240
So, um... what do we owe you?

00:09:00.360 --> 00:09:03.900
Ah? Nothing. I didn't do anything for you.

00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:06.950
I would've cooked that up with or without guests.

00:09:06.950 --> 00:09:08.820
B-but we can't just...

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:13.110
Okay, fine. I'll take 1,000 yen each.

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:14.110
What?!

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:21.070
Thank you so much, sir. We'll repay you someday.

00:09:21.610 --> 00:09:24.570
Don't even worry about it, but come again.

00:09:24.570 --> 00:09:26.820
My wife's a better cook than I am.

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:30.360
Come back next month, next year,
whenever you feel like.

00:09:41.030 --> 00:09:43.240
Shinjuku

00:09:43.650 --> 00:09:45.530
Oh, look at this, Tsutsun!

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:46.900
See?

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:48.280
Uh, yeah.

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:50.240
It looked right at me.

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:52.200
It's kind of cute.

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:53.990
It says it's a Great Buddha keychain.

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:56.780
Tsutsun, let's both buy one so we can match!

00:09:56.780 --> 00:10:00.530
You know, sometimes you have
the most incredible taste.

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:01.650
You think so?

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:07.950
The train will be arriving shortly.
Please stay behind the white line.

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:15.740
Well, see you at school.

00:10:16.070 --> 00:10:17.030
Yeah.

00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:33.030
Okay... see you later.

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:34.530
Yeah.

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:42.900
A night away from home?

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:45.360
You'd better have a very good excuse.

00:10:46.030 --> 00:10:47.110
I'm gonna go change.

00:10:47.110 --> 00:10:47.900
Hold it!

00:10:48.030 --> 00:10:49.650
It's none of your business, Chika!

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:52.070
You have to stop seeing that guy!

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:53.860
I'm so sick of hearing that.

00:10:53.860 --> 00:10:55.110
This isn't the same!

00:10:56.280 --> 00:10:58.530
Now I'm saying it for his sake.

00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:00.900
What are you going to do?

00:11:01.570 --> 00:11:04.820
What do you think is going to happen to him
when you're gone?

00:11:05.650 --> 00:11:07.450
Stop trying to make memories...

00:11:09.070 --> 00:11:10.570
and get out of his life.

00:11:11.780 --> 00:11:14.070
The responsibility is too much for you.

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:23.320
What? You only have one more month with Igarashi?

00:11:23.650 --> 00:11:24.820
Yeah.

00:11:25.570 --> 00:11:27.900
I'm sorry. I had no idea.

00:11:28.530 --> 00:11:32.070
It... it must have been hard. I guess it's still hard!

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:35.570
Yeah. So sorry if you find me freaking out.

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:39.820
I hope you'll be here for us in this last month.

00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:42.030
I will.

00:11:42.030 --> 00:11:43.650
And also, we did it.

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:44.570
What?

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:47.070
What? What? What?!

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:49.780
I-I'm sorry, you startled me.

00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:53.490
So... so how was it?

00:11:53.860 --> 00:11:55.990
I sensed the sacred mysteries of life.

00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:56.740
What?!

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:06.650
Don't tell me...

00:12:06.650 --> 00:12:08.740
Wh-what? Everything is perfectly normal.

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:11.780
Liar! Something happened,
and you're gonna tell me what it is!

00:12:11.780 --> 00:12:13.450
Stop that! What is wrong with you?!
Take that and that and that and that!

00:12:13.450 --> 00:12:15.990
Arisa's got good intuition, if nothing else.

00:12:15.990 --> 00:12:17.780
She'll know the minute I start cheating on her.

00:12:17.950 --> 00:12:20.900
Excuse me? Does this mean
you already have plans to cheat on me?

00:12:20.900 --> 00:12:22.280
That's not what I'm saying at all!

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:23.360
Yes it is!

00:12:25.650 --> 00:12:28.320
Neither of you two ever changes.

00:12:28.320 --> 00:12:30.780
It almost makes me feel like all is right with the world.

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:41.650
He finally did it, didn't he?

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:43.240
I thought so, too.

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:45.740
He is so obvious. So completely obvious.

00:12:54.030 --> 00:12:54.950
Huh?

00:12:58.530 --> 00:13:00.860
Huh? Tsutsui, you're alone?

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:04.450
Yeah. I was planning to walk home with her, but...

00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:06.400
I guess something suddenly came up.

00:13:06.400 --> 00:13:09.110
Well, it's been a while. You wanna go home together?

00:13:09.110 --> 00:13:12.070
Ayado is busy with a class representative meeting.

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:13.070
Okay.

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:21.200
So, um, Tsutsui...

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:26.030
It's too cold to go camping, but do you think
we could all do something together again?

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:26.700
Huh?

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:28.780
I-it could be anything.

00:13:29.610 --> 00:13:33.400
But I just think everyone's going to miss
Igarashi when she's gone.

00:13:33.900 --> 00:13:38.650
And of course, I consider her to be
a very good friend to me, too.

00:13:39.530 --> 00:13:42.900
So... I was hoping we could make some more memories.

00:13:43.280 --> 00:13:46.400
Yeah. You're right.

00:13:47.900 --> 00:13:48.820
I'll ask her.

00:13:55.450 --> 00:13:56.320
What is this?

00:13:56.780 --> 00:13:58.780
Why is it so hard for me to find her?

00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:00.610
Could it be...

00:14:01.030 --> 00:14:02.860
She's avoiding me?!

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:11.280
She won't respond to any of my calls or texts...

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:12.610
Why?

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:26.900
Excuse me! Where is Iroha Igarashi?

00:14:26.900 --> 00:14:28.530
Uh, I don't know.

00:14:28.530 --> 00:14:31.320
She hasn't been to school in about three days.

00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:31.900
What?!

00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:34.700
Was that Tsutsui?

00:14:36.110 --> 00:14:38.200
That's enough! It's too early for this! Who are you?!

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:41.450
Hey! Is she home?! Did something happen?!

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:47.490
Nothing happened, and she IS home.

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:48.610
Th-then...

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:52.030
But she says she doesn't want to see you. So go away.

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:54.530
What? Why not?

00:14:54.530 --> 00:14:55.780
I don't know.

00:14:55.780 --> 00:14:58.030
Wait! I really only need a second!

00:14:58.030 --> 00:14:59.450
Please let me talk to her!

00:14:59.450 --> 00:15:01.200
Give it a rest!

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:02.900
Just go away!

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:17.450
I got rid of him.

00:15:17.450 --> 00:15:19.530
And you're sure this is what you want?

00:15:19.530 --> 00:15:20.570
Yeah.

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:34.150
You! You're still here?

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:37.150
I can't just go to school with things like this.

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:40.240
Please let me wait here until she's willing to see me.

00:15:40.400 --> 00:15:42.150
No! I'll call the police!

00:15:42.150 --> 00:15:43.200
Go away!

00:15:46.280 --> 00:15:47.490
Go away!

00:15:54.110 --> 00:15:57.820
Please don't tell me... you're planning to sleep there.

00:15:57.820 --> 00:15:59.240
Don't mind me.

00:15:59.240 --> 00:16:01.530
Don't give me that! Go away!

00:16:02.280 --> 00:16:03.950
Ugh! That guy is hopeless!

00:16:03.950 --> 00:16:05.280
He's launched a full-blown stakeout!

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:08.280
I think you're going to have to turn him away yourself.

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:10.780
No, I'm not going to see him again.

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:13.990
Didn't you tell me it would be better that way?

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:17.780
But are you sure you want
to just drop him cold turkey like this?

00:16:18.070 --> 00:16:18.820
I'm sure.

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:23.990
I always knew I was going to have
to do this eventually anyway.

00:16:29.820 --> 00:16:31.990
Whew, he's finally gone...

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:45.820
What are you doing back here?

00:16:45.820 --> 00:16:48.860
Oh, it's just colder than I expected.
I had to get some supplies.

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:50.030
Well, don't!

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:51.990
Look.

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:55.990
If she really doesn't want to see me, I'm okay with that.

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:59.700
But could you let me see her so she can tell me herself?

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:19.400
Thank you!

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:31.030
Sorry, I'm coming in.

00:17:47.070 --> 00:17:48.150
So...

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:52.990
you were just going to leave,
without saying goodbye to me.

00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:58.360
Why... would you do that?

00:17:59.070 --> 00:18:00.150
Because...

00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:02.700
I didn't want to say goodbye.

00:18:03.860 --> 00:18:06.280
It wasn't supposed to turn out this way.

00:18:07.650 --> 00:18:11.320
I didn't think... I would end up loving you so much.

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:18.030
Where are you going, anyway?

00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:21.900
Does this mean we'll never see each other again?

00:18:25.610 --> 00:18:27.150
Hey, Tsutsun.

00:18:28.150 --> 00:18:31.740
Would you mind going
to the school with me, one last time?

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:43.740
This is where we officially became a couple.

00:18:44.570 --> 00:18:47.070
And you're never going to come to school again?

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:54.780
Can't we at least stay together until your last day?

00:18:55.650 --> 00:18:57.990
All our friends, even Ito would want...

00:18:57.990 --> 00:18:59.070
No.

00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:03.740
I can't really stomach the idea
of saying goodbye to everyone.

00:19:10.280 --> 00:19:12.610
Tsutsun, the thing is...

00:19:13.740 --> 00:19:15.530
there's a pesky little bug in here.

00:19:16.700 --> 00:19:18.530
I'm going to have it exterminated.

00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:23.150
You mean you...

00:19:23.780 --> 00:19:24.070
You're having
surgery...?

00:19:24.070 --> 00:19:24.150
You're having
surgery...?
You're having
surgery...?

00:19:24.150 --> 00:19:24.280
You're having
surgery...?
You're having
surgery...?

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:25.240
You're having
surgery...?

00:19:25.360 --> 00:19:27.450
We don't know if it's going to work.

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:31.610
So I might not ever get to see you again.

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:35.780
And even if it does work,
they say I might forget everything.

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:38.650
About you, about everyone.

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:41.570
I'm sorry.

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:44.610
Huh?

00:19:47.780 --> 00:19:49.280
What...

00:19:50.740 --> 00:19:52.240
is happening?

00:19:54.360 --> 00:19:58.070
Is this supposed to be some kind of test?

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:02.200
Why?

00:20:03.610 --> 00:20:05.280
Why? Why?!

00:20:07.280 --> 00:20:10.360
This ending is so much crueler
than anything I could have prepared for.

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:12.780
It's more than I can bear.

00:20:15.490 --> 00:20:17.070
There's nothing I can do.

00:20:18.280 --> 00:20:19.700
Nothing...

00:20:33.490 --> 00:20:34.740
I'm sorry.

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:36.530
Don't cry.

00:20:37.530 --> 00:20:38.610
I'm sorry.

00:20:38.610 --> 00:20:40.610
Why are you apologizing, Tsutsun?

00:20:41.450 --> 00:20:44.490
Because I had no idea.

00:20:44.490 --> 00:20:48.610
I couldn't do anything to help. I'm so sorry.

00:20:49.150 --> 00:20:50.570
It's okay.

00:20:51.780 --> 00:20:55.240
I got to meet you before it was over.

00:20:55.240 --> 00:20:58.320
God has given me so many rewards
for going through this.

00:20:59.490 --> 00:21:01.740
I'm so glad I got to meet you.

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:05.900
Thank you, Tsutsun.

00:21:11.400 --> 00:21:12.990
This is goodbye.

00:21:15.320 --> 00:21:20.780
The rhythm of the dry leaves, the season of endings,

00:21:20.780 --> 00:21:24.860
You led me by the hand

00:21:26.030 --> 00:21:36.280
The white breath is the fading future (future)

00:21:36.740 --> 00:21:54.320
Whether again or for the first time, show me your childlike face

00:21:55.490 --> 00:22:00.740
Could you meet the person you wanted to meet?

00:22:00.740 --> 00:22:05.990
Could you be the person you wanted to be?

00:22:06.110 --> 00:22:16.650
By being yourself, you helped me to be myself

00:22:16.780 --> 00:22:22.030
This day, today, when all we do is breathe,

00:22:22.030 --> 00:22:27.280
Is more wonderful than anything

00:22:27.360 --> 00:22:32.610
I don't need anything. Now let's go

00:22:32.740 --> 00:22:40.740
There's nothing to worry about
